                        "Ring lab (Mo, Oct 26 ~1:25 AM: a page to try the ring's features himself, see everything it sends, and switch SpO2 and the other measurements on and off): Settings › More screens › Ring lab. It shows the ring's connection, battery, firmware and steps; a switch per measurement (heart rate, HRV, SpO2, stress, skin temperature, blood pressure) with the last result decoded; automatic-monitoring steppers (0 to 12) and a temperature switch with a \"Read current\" button; vibration level, Find ring and notification buzz; the gestures switch with a live gesture count; the LED read, switch and effect; and a raw hex command box. The hex of every frame sits under its control. Every press goes through the same safety guard and 1-second write spacing as before; the dangerous commands stay refused.",
