                        "Ring bridge (Mo, Oct 26: \"the health app on tailscale should be able to have you control it ... one single time\"): the PC can now drive a second Bluetooth device, the MoYoung M09 smart ring, through the phone over the remote debug channel (`mglab debug send ble op=scan|connect|write|read|drain|disconnect|state`). The phone does the radio work while it is on you, so the ring's weak signal is in range; everything sent and received is kept for the PC and archived on the phone (Documents/ring-bridge). It has its own Bluetooth connection and never touches the WHOOP link. The phone refuses the ring's dangerous commands itself (reset, shutdown, restart, binding, firmware update, alarm deletes). A set-clock keep-alive every 30 s holds the link, and it reconnects on its own after a drop.",
