                    install: "installed Sat Oct 17 11:25 AM over Wi-Fi", changes: [
                        "Remote debug channel (T10012): the PC can ask the app for its logs, status, a strap history download, a sync, the night chain or a read of the strap settings, and the app answers on the PC. It listens by itself while the app runs, one command at a time, each logged in the compute log. Nothing in it writes to the strap. Needs a PC Lab restart.",
                        "The status post to the PC now includes the Raw night line, the launch timing line and the battery learner state (T10010).",
                    ]),
        ReleaseNote(version: "0.5.8.3", name: "Round 7",
                    when: "Sat Oct 17, 2026, 1:59 AM", build: "stamped at build",
                    install: "installed Sat Oct 17 2:08 AM over Wi-Fi", changes: [
                        "Background work is lighter (T9995): with the app in the background only last night is computed, in short slices with rests, so iOS no longer cuts the app off for using too much CPU; older days are done when the app is open. Sync follow-ups (T9991): a drop queued during a long upload is picked up, a stalled upload is stopped, Reset Sync keeps going if you leave the app.",
                        "Note, Sat Oct 17, 2026 (added later; the bullet above is left as written): iOS still cut the app off. Overnight the hourly background compute was ended by iOS about 3 minutes after it started (T10008), and memory warnings arrived every 6 minutes while raw optical streamed (T10009). Round 8 changed both (built, phone check pending).",
                        "PC numbers within 10 minutes of waking (T9993): when the strap says you are awake and moving, the app wakes, downloads the night, uploads it, the PC runs the night models and the results come back, with each step timed in the log. Needs a PC Lab restart.",
                        "Note, Sat Oct 17, 2026 (added later; the bullet above is left as written): this did not happen. The wake chain never fired the morning after install (T10007): the strap's awake flag holds only 1 hour, so an app opened later did not start it, and the app was not running after 6:22 AM (T10008). Round 8 changed the trigger (T10007, built, phone check pending).",
                        "The app no longer flashes \"MG not connected\" or \"PC not set up\" at launch (T10004). The strap sheet shows its last record while a download runs (T9999). The raw optical switch text is correct (T10000).",
                        "The day file is held back 30 minutes between non-manual re-uploads (T10002); this limits the repeated uploads but the root cause is not found yet.",
                        "HRV screen (T9976): every HRV method by night, deep sleep, morning 5 minutes and whole day, from the PC, with Apple's SDNN and WHOOP's history kept apart. Not yet seen on the phone.",
                        "The PC computes the HRV suite (T9990 gives hr-clean its own version entry) and Settings > About shows which algorithm map the phone follows (T9972, T9809).",
                        "One strain engine (T9987): the front page and the PC Strain panel use the same TRIMP base; the 0-21 number is labelled \"WHOOP-style scale (our mapping, not validated)\". Fitting it to WHOOP history is still open.",
                        "Battery (T9981): the time-left estimate is steadier (7-day robust fit) and learns the real extra drain of raw optical, 100 Hz motion, ECG and downloads from your own on/off log; each shows \"guessed\" until it has been on and off at least 3 hours, then \"measured over N h\".",
                        "Faster open and smoother scrolling (T23, T9904): less work on the main thread at launch and on each refresh. Needs a phone run to confirm.",
                        "Live PPG (T10005): the graph draws smoothly at a capped rate, shows a cleaned (ours) green trace, and the phone should run cooler. No 50 Hz option: no known command sets the rate.",
                        "Strap alarm fallback (T9816): if the strap alarm does not buzz, the app buzzes instead.",
                        "ECG summary (T9821): the finished reading in words: heart rate, R-R spread, signal quality, contact and rhythm class (ours, not a diagnosis).",
                        "Keep raw on the strap (T9992): a new switch, off by default, asks the strap to bank raw optical in its own history while the app is closed. Costs strap storage and battery; whether it survives a swipe-away is unknown.",
                    ]),
        ReleaseNote(version: "0.5.8.2", name: "Night fix",
                    when: "Sat Oct 17, 2026, 12:51 AM", build: "stamped at build",
                    install: "installed Sat Oct 17 12:51 AM over Wi-Fi (two compile fixes first)", changes: [
                        "Raw optical no longer switches itself off: a history download only pauses it, and it comes back by itself; your switch stays on. Live heart rate stays on with it, so iOS keeps the app awake with the phone locked.",
                        "A history download can no longer get stuck: every step has a time limit, a lost strap connection ends it, and a download quiet for 10 minutes is replaced. Before, one stuck download blocked every later one until you reopened the app.",
                        "Chunks the phone already saved are confirmed to the strap again without being saved twice; the log says how many chunks were new and how far the strap moved.",
                        "Sleep: ALG-103 is removed. Total sleep, time awake in the night and the night itself come only from the strap sleep flag (ALG-150); stages come from the stager inside the strap-asleep minutes. Time to fall asleep shows blank until there is a bed time.",
                    ]),
        ReleaseNote(version: "0.5.8.1", name: "Raw night",
                    when: "Thu Oct 15, 2026, 11:58 PM", build: "stamped at build",
                    install: "installed Fri Oct 16 12:02 AM over Wi-Fi (first try 11:58 PM stalled, nothing changed)", changes: [
                        "Raw optical (R20) and 100 Hz motion (R21) that you have switched on keep running all night with the phone locked or face down. Checked: they are sent again after every reconnect (also after iOS restarts the app for Bluetooth), nothing in lock or background stops them, and raw motion has no time limit when its switch is on.",
                        "Raw optical comes back on by itself after a history download. The download watchdog can pause it so the download finishes; before, it then stayed off until you toggled the switch.",
                        "Settings › Usage › Strap in the background has a new \"Raw night\" line for the morning: minutes of R20 and R21 received, gaps over 2 minutes with their times, and strap disconnects and reconnects.",
                        "The version label is 0.5.8.1; the iOS short version stays 0.5.8 (iOS allows three numbers).",
                    ]),
        ReleaseNote(version: "0.5.8", name: "Sync drain",
                    when: "Thu Oct 15, 2026, 11:06 PM", build: "stamped at build",
                    install: "installed Thu Oct 15 11:07 PM over Wi-Fi", changes: [
                        "Sync now and opening the app keep sending until nothing is waiting (they used to stop after 25-30 s, so \"2 days not on PC, 2.5 MB waiting\" never cleared). Leaving the app no longer cuts an upload off.",
                        "A half-sent day carries on where it stopped; days are only resent when their data really changed; streams and raw data no longer wait behind resent days; Apple Health batches the PC already has are not sent again.",
                        "If a sync still stops early it says so: \"stopped, N MB left\" in Strap & sync and a new Last sync row.",
                        "Background sync tries every 5 minutes while the strap is live, instead of once an hour.",
                        "Raw optical and 100 Hz motion keep running when you leave the Live tab, until you switch them off (still off by default).",
                        "The Burned ring shows our calories from strap heart rate (estimate). WHOOP-cloud and Apple numbers show only as labelled comparisons.",
                        "PC: primary sleep number on the current SleepECG model; SleepECG files each night under the day it ended; PC scores use your imported history, skin temperature and measured max HR when your own nights are too few; honest method lists and sleep panel labels.",
                    ]),
        ReleaseNote(version: "0.5.7", name: "Sleep V3",
                    when: "Thu Oct 15, 2026, 7:40 PM", build: "stamped at build",
                    install: "V3 installed Thu Oct 15 8:11 PM over Wi-Fi (V1 6:06 PM crashed at launch; V2 6:28 PM crashed on Sync now / permission check)", changes: [
                        "V3: no more crash on launch, on coming back to the app, or on Sync now. The app asks Apple Health about permissions once, for the safe types only (measurements, categories, workouts, ECG); the newer kinds say \"not in this build (being made safe)\" until they are.",
                        "V3: Apple Health is read when each type should be: heart rate, steps, HRV, breathing, SpO2 hourly; sleep, wrist temperature and the night's SpO2/HRV/breathing right after you wake; weight, VO2 max, resting HR, walking daily; the rest on Sync now. Sync now no longer pulls all of Apple Health at once (25 s / 60 pages per run, off the main thread, resumes).",
                        "V3: opens fast: Today shows saved values at once and computes in the background (last night and today first).",
                        "V3: Today's recovery shows a number: an estimate while the baseline is short, its baseline topped up with WHOOP's numbers from your export (HRV) and Apple's numbers where the unit matches, labelled \"baseline includes N imported nights\".",
                        "V3: a PC sleep number is shown only if it matches the strap's night (covers 80% of it, total within +-50%); otherwise the strap number stays. PC sleep models now take the night from the strap's sleep flag.",
                        "V3: PC results flow again: one PC result the phone refused (Apple active calories labelled \"apple\") stopped every sync after Oct 14; the phone now accepts that label and a refused result can never stall the rest.",
                        "V2: 0.5.7 V1 closed itself right after opening. Starting Apple Health change-watching on the new Health types made HealthKit throw. Now only the four kinds 0.5.6 watched are watched (the newer kinds are still read on every sync); vision prescriptions and CDA documents are skipped (they need one-by-one permission).",
                        "Sleep: the strap's own sleep flag decides asleep/awake and the total, after the night, padded at both ends; stages stay inside it. When the PC has a result for the night, Today and Sleep show the PC numbers (labelled); the phone estimate only stands in until then or when the PC can't be reached or is more than 30 minutes late after you wake. Today never says \"Past your bedtime\", \"Bedtime\" or \"Wind down\" while you're asleep or in the hour after you wake (\"Asleep since\", \"Awake since\" instead); a brief awakening doesn't flip it.",
                        "Recovery for today never shows WHOOP's number; WHOOP only fills past days.",
                        "Every frame the strap sends is now archived raw and synced to the PC (database v8).",
                        "Your medication, supplement and drink lists: add, edit and remove in Settings; pick them in Log (\"From your list\"); logged items reach the PC. No supplements are pre-filled.",
                        "Focus: a focus window (late morning, after waking up properly) and a \"second wind\" (evening), both from your own wake time and sleep timing (estimate). The old method is kept beside it.",
                        "Heart rate is cleaned before resting HR, strain and calories use it (impossible values out, single spikes removed, still and good-quality seconds for resting HR); the old raw method can still be picked.",
                        "Today's strain, stress, sleep and sleep consistency in WHOOP's terms; past days use WHOOP's own numbers, both shown when both exist.",
                        "Algorithms can be switched from the PC without an app update (the PC says which method is shown for each number).",
                        "Strap timer: the row says \"armed on strap\" only after the strap confirms it, or \"not armed on strap: why\"; it retries; every step is logged; the phone alert is time-sensitive. (The strap may not fire timer slots on firmware 50.42; the phone alert is the backstop.)",
                        "Live ECG: start, 5-second lead-in, 60 seconds recorded, filtered/raw view, heart rate, save and send to the PC.",
                        "Apple Health: every type is read and sent to the PC, nothing dropped; Settings shows each type's status and last sample.",
                        "Phone use (estimate): unlocked time and when, per day. App alive/killed log and a ping the PC shows.",
                        "Custom date range on the period picker. Keyboard closes when you tap outside it. Dial: hold and slide on the outer ring.",
                        "PC: models run at their proper times on their own (sleep models when the night closes, trend models daily); a \"Last PC pass\" line; a methods viewer page (PC browser / iPad view-only); pulse-shape values now reach the PC so BP and more MS outputs can run; chat from the phone goes to OpenCode on the PC, sandboxed.",
                        "Versions: release R9 (versions/bom.json); every algorithm change is listed in versions/HISTORY.md.",
                    ]),
        ReleaseNote(version: "0.5.6", name: "Health",
                    when: "Wed Oct 14, 2026, 12:25 PM", build: "stamped at build",
                    install: "installed Oct 14 (corrected Oct 15 6:10 PM; this line said NOT INSTALLED)", changes: [
                        "Today shows the right night and recomputes after an install: a rest that ends on another day is never today's night (its sleep rows are blank and say why), the first launch of a new build computes today again, and a run stuck for more than 20 minutes is dropped and redone. Settings › Usage › Compute log lists each run so a hang leaves a trace. \"Stress onsets (count)\" is now a proper row in the Stress group.",
                        "Today's \"models not running\" now says why: missing input, waiting for data, or no value (with the model's own reason); not-built and blocked models keep their own rows and their own count.",
                        "Recovery falls back to WHOOP's recovery for last night (labelled) when the strap has no night of its own. Max HR (Tanaka) is recomputed when the birth date reaches the phone quietly, not only when you type it.",
                        "Strain and max-HR cards: the Strain card asks the PC up to today and fills days the phone has no WHOOP value for; Max HR has WHOOP export and Apple Health daily-max rows.",
                        "Sync never needs you: one refused key no longer stops sync (it says \"1 of 3\" and tries again; only the third in a row asks you to pair again), retries wait 1, 2, 5, 15, then every 60 minutes (example steps, not measured), and the state survives a restart. Settings has a sync panel with Sync now and Reset, and an alert when the PC is not receiving. The phone keeps its queue until the PC confirms receipts.",
                        "Strap timer alarm: starting a timer also writes it into a strap alarm slot (2 to 6) so the strap buzzes with the app in the background, up to 2 minutes; cancelling clears the slot; a reconnect re-checks running timers. Double tap stops the timer. Your full pattern (4 buzzes, 1 second gap, 4 more) only runs while the app is alive.",
                        "Optical saturated is filled: the strap's own per-second bit, else a count of raw-optical seconds pinned at the limit (an estimate, ALG-144 gates), blank with a reason naming both when neither exists. pSNR and log-variance are decoded, untested.",
                        "What's running (Settings › Usage): today's compute runs, sync attempts, live heart-rate and raw optical switch-on time and background tasks iOS started. It starts counting when this build first runs and starts no work.",
                        "PC sleep and heart-rate models (SleepECG, wav2sleep, BeliefPPG) are installed in their own Python environments and their results show beside ALG-120. All are labelled estimate; none is validated against a sleep study or chest ECG. wav2sleep needs a night with raw PPG recorded all night.",
                        "Apple Health is read by the app itself in the background (read-only, one permission sheet) and sent to the PC with no Shortcut or export. Settings › Apple Health shows last read, last reached the PC and samples queued. A refused batch stays on the phone.",
                        "Apple import v8 (PC): Watch ECG recordings, a device-aware duplicate key, per-minute heart rate and per-5-minute HRV series, and the Watch sleep stages by clock time (30-second grid, a gap stays a gap, never 0).",
                        "Still to check on the phone: the strap alarm buzzing with the app killed, the double-tap stop, the Health permission prompt on first open, and background delivery of Health samples to the PC. The screen and app wiring (ios/App, ios/UI) is compiled but not package-tested; no strap alarm or command was sent from here.",
                    ]),
        ReleaseNote(version: "0.5.5", name: "Clean",
                    when: "Wed Oct 14, 2026, 11:10 AM", build: "stamped at build",
                    install: "NOT INSTALLED", changes: [
                        "Timer buzz with the app in the background: a timer now also goes into one of the strap's own alarm slots (2 to 6, never your wake alarm), is cleared when you cancel it, and is checked again when the strap reconnects. The strap holds at most 2 minutes of buzzing, so your 4 / pause / 4 loop only runs while the app is open. Whether a double tap stops the strap's own alarm is not confirmed. Built and tested in packages; not tried on the strap.",
                        "Bedtime and stuck compute: a bedtime is never a daytime \"tonight\" any more, and a compute run that went stale is abandoned instead of hanging. Stale-run write races, per-night daylight-saving offsets and daytime sleep after a schedule change are fixed too. Built and tested in packages; not yet on the phone.",
                        "Explore groups and registry: HRV, Biological age and Rough night groups show every method they compute (Rough night compares two methods and never averages them); group rows open their own screen; a blank shows a dash and a \"why\"; Today's recovery follows the method you chose and says so when it has no result; \"Night screens\" is part of Sleep; weight, body fat, lean mass and BMI from Apple Health are kept and listed under Activity.",
                        "Readable values and honest periods: times read as a local date and 12-hour time (not 1791171598.0); recovery drivers read \"3 of 4 in range · out: HRV\"; key points list their sentences; labs show their newest draw whatever the period; aerobic base no longer mixes two measures.",
                        "Day values: a VO2 max estimate from your heart rates (Uth, labelled estimate) fills the Keytel calories row so it no longer waits for a waist measurement; strain is stored blank (with the reason) when our model says 0 but WHOOP logged a strain that day; WHOOP and Apple daily max HR have their own rows (one sample can be a spike, never used as your maximum); the Vape row's heart-rate line now has data; one steps rule; blanks name their reason, no fake zeros.",
                        "Live: the pulse wave box draws the raw optical wave (raw counts, decoded, untested) with the real reason when empty; a cleaned wave (ALG-144, research, estimate) sits beside it with a quality chip; a pace and freeze watch on Live. The cleaning and quality step is not tuned against ECG yet.",
                        "Settings › Command test has a raw optical (PPG) test block: one on/off switch, each slot drawn, every flip logged. Decoded, untested on your strap.",
                        "Notification taps: tapping the wear notification opens Strap & sync.",
                        "Strap timer alarms (slots 2-6) are built but NOT sent to the strap.",
                        "PC Lab never drops data: past active calories kept, blank reasons stored, unknown kinds parked, a drop audit. PC sleep and heart-rate models (SleepECG, wav2sleep, BeliefPPG) are written but not installed yet: the separate Python environment is not created, and all their output will be labelled estimate.",
                        "Settings › Export also writes kv/kv.json: the phone's key-value area (profile, retention setting, read positions) with sizes; the install secret is listed but its bytes are withheld. Nothing is deleted or changed.",
                        "Stale docs and comments corrected (bug 29), including the model catalogue: ALG-045 (gait symmetry) is marked X, since only its Apple Health data path exists and nothing is computed from it.",
                        "Not yet checked on the phone: all of the above is compiled or package-tested only; the app-target code (screens, Export wiring, Live, notification taps) has not been run on a device, and no strap alarm or command was sent.",
                    ]),
        ReleaseNote(version: "0.5.4", name: "Rings",
                    when: "Tue Oct 13, 2026, 9:09 AM", build: "202610130909",
                    install: "INSTALLED over Wi-Fi (Tailscale), Tue Oct 13, 2026, 9:10 AM, build 202610130909", changes: [
                        "Today looks like 0.5.3 again, softened: serif headline, letter badges and mono receipts kept; day is a softer cream, night a darker green; only labelled buttons are solid, the rest are quiet. Tiles no longer wrap one word per line.",
                        "The sundial keeps its 24-hour face (12, 18, 00, 06) and now has WHOOP-style inner rings: Strain, Recovery, Sleep and Stress (Burned and Eaten when on). Tap a ring, a night/workout/nap arc or a mark on the rim (vape, medication, caffeine, focus) to open a sheet with its own numbers. A key under the dial has one chip per ring and mark kind. Recovery ring = metrics in range of those scored. Vape and medication heart-rate effects are estimates.",
                        "Live, Log, Explore, Settings and the sheets got the same skin (colours, type, spacing, button weights). Settings is in five clusters. The \"Working on\" line is one quiet line; tap it to open Settings. Sample data has a slim banner.",
                        "Everything built since 0.5.3 is in this build (the T-list work: medication presets, cuff calibration, skin-type quiz, vape analysis, command test page, strap broadcast, workout trends, sleep-debt change, Strap-vs-ours lab, and more). Most of it has been compiled but not yet opened on a phone.",
                    ]),
        ReleaseNote(version: "0.5.3", name: "Steadier",
                    when: "Mon Oct 12, 2026, 6:50 PM", build: "202610121850",
                    install: "INSTALLED over Wi-Fi (Tailscale), Mon Oct 12, 2026, 6:48 PM, build 202610121850 (the build number was stamped as 6:50 PM before the build finished; the real signing time was about 6:47 PM)", changes: [
                        "Alarms no longer crashes when you open it: each section of the screen is built on its own, so the screen is no longer one huge nest that overflowed the stack (T106). Built and compiled; not yet opened on a phone.",
                        "The \"off wrist\" flag no longer stays stuck after the strap is back on your wrist: if no beats arrive for a while the flag is dropped, and a beat clears it at once (T110).",
                        "Battery days-left now counts what the strap is doing for you (raw optical, motion, ECG, the alarm). It says \"calibrating\" until the per-feature drain figures are measured, because they are placeholders today (T107, T59).",
                        "Profile: weight in pounds, height in feet and inches (\"155 lb\", \"5 feet 8 inches\", \"5'8\"). The app still stores kg and cm. A bare height number is refused because 58 could be inches or cm (T3, T111).",
                        "Profile fills itself from the PC or Apple Health without a tap; if it cannot, it stays quiet. Estimates with no spread read \"est.\" (T27, T29, T132).",
                        "Fewer CPU kills (first half): the app rests between night and day stages (share 0.8 and a pause of 2 s or less when you are waiting; 0.4 and 5 s or less for background work), and both pulse dots are capped at 30 fps (T140). Not yet measured on a phone.",
                    ]),
        ReleaseNote(version: "0.5.2", name: "Hand back",
                    when: "Sun Oct 11, 2026, 11:56 PM", build: "202610120006",
                    install: "INSTALLED over Wi-Fi, Mon Oct 12, 2026, 3:58 PM", changes: [
                        "Live › Research › \"Test: read history without deleting\": about a minute with the strap connected. The app asks the strap for its history, keeps the first piece on the phone, and does not tell the strap it may drop it; then it asks again and checks the strap still offers the same piece. You see the strap's read and delete markers before and after, so you can tell whether a read without confirming leaves your data on the strap. The normal history download waits while it runs. Decoded, untested until you run it.",
                        "Strap & sync › \"Hand the strap back to WHOOP\" (leave no trace): on, HealthApp puts back what it changed on the strap (the deep-data setting enable_r22_packets to its earlier value, the strap alarm it set), stops raw optical, raw motion and ECG, then disconnects and stays off so the WHOOP app can have the strap. Nothing already collected is deleted, on the phone or the PC. Off: HealthApp connects again, your switches apply, the strap alarm re-arms, and the deep-data setting goes back on through its confirm sheet.",
                    ]),
        ReleaseNote(version: "0.5.1", name: "Recovery fix",
